// Generated by scripts/restructure-by-construct.
// Per-construct DSL layout: every <kind>s.memql file in a domain
// holds every construct of that kind in the domain. The companion
// files cover the other construct kinds.

// killSwitchSuspendsRunningPlans is GONE (memql#5053, follow-up memql#5066).
//
// It suspended a user's running computer-use Plans when
// preferences.computerUseEnabled flipped false. It went with the Plan
// concepts rather than being ported, on three findings:
//
//   - it never fired. Its query's own doc comment recorded that
//     `args.event.payload.id ?? ""` reaches argument validation as an
//     unevaluated CoalesceExpr (memql#2870);
//   - its predicate was `computerUseScope != null`, a Plan field with no run
//     equivalent, so a port would either cancel every in-flight run of that
//     user or add a field to v1:work:run to carry a scope it does not need;
//   - the ENFORCED control is untouched and is elsewhere:
//     integrations/agent/worker/dispatch.go reads the flag before EVERY
//     dispatch and returns deny with `kill_switch_engaged`, failing closed on
//     a lookup error.
//
// Flipping the switch still stops all NEW computer-use calls. What is gone is
// the in-flight half, which never worked; memql#5066 decides whether it is
// wanted at all.

// workerInvocationRetentionSweep
// ===============================
//
// Daily 02:30 UTC sweep. Soft-deletes worker-invocation rows older
// than WORKER_INVOCATION_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90). Per-user
// invocation queries already filter on the isNotDeleted trait (see
// dsl/worker/queries.memql) so the rows disappear from UIs the moment
// the soft-delete lands.
//
// Different from auditEventRetentionSweep on the identity side
// (default 365) because per-call telemetry is high-volume and
// security signals are not. Operators tune via the
// WORKER_INVOCATION_RETENTION_DAYS env var.
//
// MemQL parser limitations:
//   - The filter side of expiredWorkerInvocations can't push
//     the duration math into the query (no `>` operator on
//     datetime). Per-row gating uses
//       addDuration(item.createdAt, "P{retention}D") < now
/// Daily 02:30 UTC sweep: soft-delete worker-invocation rows past WORKER_INVOCATION_RETENTION_DAYS.
/// decide (pure) returns the candidate rows; window reads the retention var; the forEach apply
/// gates each row on createdAt + P{N}D < now (#2256/#2254 evaluator fix) and soft-deletes it.
@trigger(schedule="0 30 2 * * *")
automation workerInvocationRetentionSweep {
  step decide {
    logic workerInvocationRetentionSweep ( event: event )
  }
  step apply {
    forEach item in decide.result {
      softDeleteWorkerInvocation {
        invocationId: item.id
      }
    }
  }
}
